Fork: read-only telemetry exporter

Build

  This repository currently requires Go 1.25.6 or newer as declared in go.mod.
  If Go is installed globally:

      make

  If using a custom Go toolchain that is not already on PATH, prefix commands
  with that toolchain's bin directory:

      PATH=/path/to/go/bin:$PATH make

  Run tests:

      go test ./...
      go test -race ./...

One-shot diagnostics

  On many Linux hosts, /dev/i2c-* is owned by root and requires sudo:

      sudo ./bin/sus-check

  A successful check prints detected compatible GPUs, NVML index, PCI sysfs
  path, selected /dev/i2c-N device, total NVML GPU load, total connector draw,
  balance ratio, and all six pin voltage/current/power readings.

  If access fails, inspect the device printed by sus-check:

      ls -l /dev/i2c-N
      lsmod | grep i2c_dev
      sudo modprobe i2c-dev
      nvidia-smi

  Bus numbers can vary by host. Any udev rule must match the actual device on
  that host.

Prometheus exporter

  Run locally:

      sudo ./bin/sus-exporter --listen=127.0.0.1:9479

  Validate locally:

      curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:9479/healthz
      curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:9479/metrics
      curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:9479/metrics | promtool check metrics

  The default listen address is loopback-only because the exporter may need to
  run as root for i2c access. To scrape it from a central Prometheus host, bind
  it deliberately to a LAN IP and restrict TCP/9479 to the Prometheus host with
  firewall rules.

Metrics

  sus_pin_voltage_volts{gpu_uuid,gpu_index,pin}
  sus_pin_current_amps{gpu_uuid,gpu_index,pin}
  sus_pin_power_watts{gpu_uuid,gpu_index,pin}
  sus_connector_power_watts{gpu_uuid,gpu_index}
  sus_gpu_nvml_power_watts{gpu_uuid,gpu_index}
  sus_pin_min_power_watts{gpu_uuid,gpu_index}
  sus_pin_max_power_watts{gpu_uuid,gpu_index}
  sus_pin_balance_ratio{gpu_uuid,gpu_index}
  sus_device_read_success{gpu_uuid,gpu_index}
  sus_scrape_errors_total{reason}

  Do not expect a host label from the exporter. Prometheus adds the scrape
  target as the instance label. Add site/rack/role labels in Prometheus scrape
  configuration if needed.

Install exporter service

  Install only after local validation:

      sudo install -m 0755 bin/sus-exporter /usr/local/bin/sus-exporter
      sudo install -m 0755 bin/sus-check /usr/local/bin/sus-check
      sudo install -m 0644 install/sus-exporter.service /etc/systemd/system/sus-exporter.service
      sudo systemctl daemon-reload
      sudo systemctl enable --now sus-exporter
      systemctl status sus-exporter

  The provided service runs /usr/local/bin/sus-exporter on 127.0.0.1:9479. It
  uses basic hardening but does not set PrivateDevices=true because the service
  needs access to /dev/i2c-N and NVIDIA device files.

Central Prometheus scrape example

  After each exporter is explicitly exposed to the LAN and firewalled:

      scrape_configs:
        - job_name: sus-exporter
          scrape_interval: 5s
          static_configs:
            - targets:
                - gpu-host-a.lan:9479
                - gpu-host-b.lan:9479

Initial alert rule examples

  These thresholds are starting points for observation, not final safety
  science. They should be tuned after collecting baseline data from all hosts.

      groups:
        - name: sus-connector-alerts
          rules:
            - alert: SusPinPowerWarning
              expr: sus_pin_power_watts > 105
              for: 1m
              labels:
                severity: warning
              annotations:
                summary: ASUS Astral pin power warning on {{ $labels.instance }} pin {{ $labels.pin }}
                description: A 12V-2x6 pin has exceeded 105 W for 1 minute.
            - alert: SusPinPowerCritical
              expr: sus_pin_power_watts > 110
              for: 15s
              labels:
                severity: critical
              annotations:
                summary: ASUS Astral pin power critical on {{ $labels.instance }} pin {{ $labels.pin }}
                description: A 12V-2x6 pin has exceeded 110 W for 15 seconds.
            - alert: SusPinCurrentCritical
              expr: sus_pin_current_amps > 9.2
              for: 15s
              labels:
                severity: critical
              annotations:
                summary: ASUS Astral pin current critical on {{ $labels.instance }} pin {{ $labels.pin }}
                description: A 12V-2x6 pin current reading has exceeded 9.2 A for 15 seconds.
            - alert: SusPinVoltageLow
              expr: sus_pin_voltage_volts < 11.4
              for: 15s
              labels:
                severity: warning
              annotations:
                summary: ASUS Astral pin voltage low on {{ $labels.instance }} pin {{ $labels.pin }}
                description: A 12V pin voltage reading has stayed below 11.4 V for 15 seconds.
            - alert: SusPinImbalanceCritical
              expr: sus_pin_balance_ratio < 0.75 and sus_connector_power_watts > 300
              for: 15s
              labels:
                severity: critical
              annotations:
                summary: ASUS Astral connector load imbalance on {{ $labels.instance }}
                description: Minimum pin power divided by maximum pin power is below 0.75 while connector draw is above 300 W.
            - alert: SusDeviceReadFailure
              expr: sus_device_read_success == 0
              for: 30s
              labels:
                severity: critical
              annotations:
                summary: sus-exporter cannot read GPU telemetry on {{ $labels.instance }}
                description: The exporter is reachable but cannot read one ASUS Astral GPU.
            - alert: SusExporterDown
              expr: up{job="sus-exporter"} == 0
              for: 30s
              labels:
                severity: critical
              annotations:
                summary: sus-exporter is down on {{ $labels.instance }}
                description: Prometheus cannot scrape ASUS Astral pin telemetry from this host.

Email notification

  Email belongs in Alertmanager, not in sus-exporter. Configure SMTP credentials,
  grouping, repeat intervals, and silences in Alertmanager when ready.

Upstream integration (October 5, 2026)

  Merged upstream mainster through d54b255. The fork retains its read-only
  exporter and snapshot API. Discovery does not query optional power or clock
  control capabilities. Only an explicit mitigation call queries those APIs.
  susd -u now uses amperes (default 8.5), not watts. The old -m imbalance flag
  was removed upstream. Review old service arguments before using susd.
  susd changes GPU limits and clocks. Installing sus-exporter does not enable
  susd. Monitor deployment and Discord rules live in agents-homelab.
